========================================
FIREBASE REALTIME DATABASE SETUP (ANDROID)
========================================

1. CREATE FIREBASE PROJECT
--------------------------
- Open https://console.firebase.google.com
- Click "Add Project"
- Project Name: TestDemo
- Disable Google Analytics (optional)
- Finish project creation


2. ADD ANDROID APP TO FIREBASE
------------------------------
- Open Firebase Project → Project Settings
- Click "Add App" → Android
- Enter Package Name:
    com.androidtutorials.myapplication
- Register App
- Download file:
    google-services.json
- Place file at:
    app/google-services.json


3. CONFIGURE GRADLE (PROJECT LEVEL)
----------------------------------
File: build.gradle (Project)

Add Google services plugin:

buildscript {
    dependencies {
        classpath "com.google.gms:google-services:4.4.0"
    }
}


4. CONFIGURE GRADLE (APP LEVEL)
------------------------------
File: build.gradle (Module: app)

plugins {
    id "com.google.gms.google-services"
}

dependencies {
    implementation platform("com.google.firebase:firebase-bom:32.7.0")
    implementation "com.google.firebase:firebase-database"
}

→ Sync Gradle


5. CREATE REALTIME DATABASE
---------------------------
- Firebase Console → Realtime Database
- Click "Create Database"
- Location: us-central1
- Start in TEST MODE


6. SET DATABASE RULES (TEST MODE)
--------------------------------
Firebase Console → Realtime Database → Rules

{
  "rules": {
    ".read": true,
    ".write": true
  }
}


7. FIREBASE AUTO INITIALIZATION
-------------------------------
- Firebase initializes automatically using:
    google-services.json

Verify in Logcat:
FirebaseApp initialization successful


8. JETPACK COMPOSE UI
--------------------
- Button placed at center of screen
- Button triggers Firebase write operation

@Composable
fun sendDataUI() {
    Box(
        modifier = Modifier.fillMaxSize(),
        contentAlignment = Alignment.Center
    ) {
        Button(onClick = { sendDataToFireBase() }) {
            Text("Send Data")
        }
    }
}


9. FIREBASE WRITE LOGIC
----------------------
IMPORTANT:
- getReference() takes PATH, not URL

private fun sendDataToFireBase() {
    val database = FirebaseDatabase.getInstance()
    val ref = database.getReference("Users")

    val user = mapOf(
        "name" to "Vinay TS",
        "age" to 28,
        "City" to "Bangalore"
    )

    ref.push().setValue(user)
}


10. SET CONTENT IN ACTIVITY
---------------------------
override fun onCreate(savedInstanceState: Bundle?) {
    super.onCreate(savedInstanceState)

    setContent {
        sendDataUI()
    }
}


